Article 4 (Relationship to Compulsory Execution, etc.)
Registration of establishment of sectional superficies completed under Article 2 or registration of establishment of sectional superficies that was the subject matter of expropriation under Article 3 (hereinafter referred to as "registration of establishment of sectional superficies") shall not be cancelled even in any of the following cases: <Amended on September 28, 2009; February 2, 2017; and January 9, 2019.>
1. Where registration of transfer of ownership resulting from an auction or public auction is requested based on a registration of a decision to commence compulsory auction, registration of a security interest such as a maximum-amount mortgage, registration of attachment, or registration of provisional attachment completed before the registration of establishment of sectional superficies;
2. Where a creditor who registered a provisional disposition before the registration of establishment of sectional superficies applies for registration of transfer of ownership, cancellation of registration of transfer of ownership, cancellation of registration of preservation of ownership, or registration of establishment of superficies, a chonsegwon right, or a leasehold right, designating the debtor subject to the provisional disposition as the person obligated to register;
3. Where an application is made for definitive registration of transfer of ownership or definitive registration of establishment of superficies, a chonsegwon right, or a leasehold right based on provisional registration completed before the registration of establishment of sectional superficies.
